=== p2-windows · W7 · page:maps/TemperatureImpact (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:maps/TemperatureImpact   kind=page   web route=/temperature-impact
Web source  : web/src/features/maps/pages/TemperatureImpactPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload installed — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder),
  <Name>.Source.cs (generated-client feed, ADR-004) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "TemperatureImpactPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Maps" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("TemperatureImpact", already in
  RouteTable.cs under RouteGroup.MapsLocation).
- The manifest page record carries no dataSources, but the web page does fetch GET /analytics/temperature-impact
  and its four declared states are real, so the view-model reads samples through an injected
  ITemperatureImpactFeed (default EmptyTemperatureImpactFeed → empty state; TemperatureImpactClientFeed binds the
  generated operation get_api_v1_analytics_temperature_impact via Operations.Analytics.TemperatureImpact). The
  loading/empty/error/success branch precedence mirrors the web data lifecycle.
- SI cutover (ADR / unit-conversion.instructions): outside_temp (°C SI) is converted at the display boundary via
  UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi; efficiency Wh/km → Wh/mi via the web's KM_PER_MILE factor (no
  convertEfficiencyFromSI helper exists, matching the web inline note). Nothing non-SI is stored/computed.
- The web's per-point scatter fill (bucket colour) is rendered as one Fluent scatter series named via
  tempImpact.scatterName ("Drives") to preserve the series-name parity; bucket colour is conveyed instead through
  the line chart + the optimal-analysis badges (Fluent-native, not web pixel-cloning per ADR-005).
- The in-page web VehicleSelect action is the shell's global header picker on native (sibling W7 pages do the
  same); the header carries a TsDataFreshness chip (ADR-013). The web AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative is a
  separate already-ported shared-surface parity unit (gated off by ai_mode by default) and is intentionally not
  re-embedded here — it is tracked under its own unit, not this page's 8 panels.
- All 22 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw (translation.tempImpact.* +
  translation.common.noData + translation.error.loadFailed + translation.temperature.title); the surface resolves
  them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (no new catalog rows required). The optimalDesc /
  optimalDelta / tipOptimal templates use the resw's {0}.. placeholders via string.Format (web {{var}} → {N}).
- Test project (net10.0, no WinUI host) Compile-links the three Microsoft.UI-free sources
  (Model/Source/ViewModel) in TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (path-sorted between TemperatureGauges and
  TemperatureMetricCards); the bare WinUI view is exercised by the app build.

